
Trading view ICT tools

DeliveryEngine.txt is not mine.
it's from the great Nuno.

Workflow (read this first)
==========================

The Mac checkout (/Users/nemo/u/trade/tvsrc) is the working copy.

1. git pull before changing anything.
2. Change the sources on the Mac. Regenerate the derived files
   (below), port the change to ninja/ and tradovate/ when the
   source has a port, update the md5 in the port header, and
   update the manuals (md and PDF).
3. git commit and git push from the Mac.
4. Only then, and only if Francisco decides so, update the
   TradingView scripts from the pushed commit: see
   tools/tradingview-update.md (save, update the 15m pane, save
   the ICTmany template, load it on the other panes; publishing
   needs his OK on the release notes).

Do not change files on the Mac by copying them in from another
clone without committing: it leaves the Mac checkout out of step
with git and the next pull conflicts. A Claude working from the
cloud clone commits and pushes there, then brings the Mac up to
date through git (pull), not by copying files.

Generated files (reminders)
===========================

Run everything from the tvsrc folder. Never edit a generated file by
hand: edit its source and regenerate.

FVGs (source FVGS+IFVG+OTE.txt, i.e. FVGs+IFVG+OTE5):

	python3 tools/mkfvgderiv.py
		writes ICTblocks.txt and FVGS+IFVG+OTE4.txt.
		Markers in the source: //#cut T ... //#end drops the lines
		from derivative T (ote4, blk, or sw for both); //#T code
		keeps "code" only in derivative T.

	FVGS+IFVG+OTE+PL.txt is not generated: apply the same changes by
	hand (it uses dO/dH/dL/dC instead of open/high/low/close).

Levels (source ICTlevels.txt):

	python3 tools/mklevelsderiv.py
		writes ICTgaps.txt, ICTday.txt, NWOGs.txt, NDOGs.txt and RTHOGs.txt.

ICTScalp (ICTScalp.txt, an indicator, TradingView name ICTScalp):

	Edited by hand. ICTScalpStrategy.txt (TradingView name "ICTScalp
	strategy") is generated from it and must be kept in sync: after
	changing ICTScalp.txt run

		python3 tools/mkstrategy.py ICTScalp.txt ICTScalpStrategy.txt

	and save both on TradingView. The strategy has the same code, a
	strategy() declaration, and the orders at the "strategy orders"
	mark of ICTScalp.txt (keep it). Since the HTF bias / LTF entry
	rework (25 Nov 2026) ICTScalp15.txt, ICTscalpHTFFVGs.txt and
	ICTScalpSes.txt (and tools/mk15.py, mkhtf.py, mkses.py) are no
	longer maintained and do not match it.

Ports (ICTlevels, ICTcotas and FVGS+IFVG+OTE):

	ninja/<name>.cs and tradovate/<name>.js (FVGS+IFVG+OTE is
	FVGSIFVGOTE) are hand ports. After changing the Pine source,
	port the change and update the source md5 in the port header:

	md5 ICTlevels.txt	(md5sum on Linux)

PDF manuals (doc/), from the doc folder, for each document d:

	t=$(head -1 $d.md | sed 's/^# *//')
	pandoc $d.md -s --css manual.css --embed-resources \
		--metadata pagetitle="$t" -o /tmp/$d.html
	chrome --headless --no-pdf-header-footer \
		--print-to-pdf=$d.pdf /tmp/$d.html

	On the Mac "chrome" is
	"/Applications/Google Chrome.app/Contents/MacOS/Google Chrome".
